WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:19.220
[Sawing and hammering wood]

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.800
[Narrator:] In Latin America, a child is 
dead.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.433
Two months old, the youngest of eight children.

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:36.266
She was a casualty of poverty.

00:00:36.266 --> 00:00:40.532
Another mouth to feed in a family where already 
there was too little to eat.

00:00:40.533 --> 00:00:43.899
She died of protein deficiency and malnutrition.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:48.033
And her father who worked in another town did 
not come to her funeral.

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:50.066
He could not afford to make the trip.

00:00:50.066 --> 00:01:24.966
[Music and singing]

00:01:24.966 --> 00:01:27.632
This instance of death is not unique.

00:01:27.633 --> 00:01:31.866
In countries throughout the developing 
world, the death of little children

00:01:31.866 --> 00:01:34.932
is one of the daily tragedies of life.

00:01:34.933 --> 00:01:52.099
[Music and singing]

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:57.100
Though we usually think of the 
problem of an exploding population in 
terms such as

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:03.866
economic development, overcrowding, 
underemployment, ecology, education, 
maternal health,

00:02:03.866 --> 00:02:17.332
and personal freedom, it has come 
down for these people on this day to a 
matter of life and death.

00:02:17.333 --> 00:02:21.299
[The people prepare a gravesite.]

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.666
[Dr. Madrigal:] Children dying from 
starvation in underdeveloped countries

00:02:24.666 --> 00:02:30.999
and children dying in the wars, there is 
not much difference.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.633
They are both murder.

00:02:32.633 --> 00:02:37.999
I'm scared about the population in the 
whole world, but especially in El 
Salvador,

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:44.866
which is a place where I live, where my 
children are, my wife, my work, 
everything.

00:02:44.866 --> 00:02:48.832
And it's, I'm scared, of course. That's why I'm 
working here.

00:02:48.833 --> 00:02:50.233
[Interviewer:] Is it that desperate?

00:02:50.233 --> 00:02:56.199
[Dr. Madrigal:] Yes. I think it's 
desperate, the situation, but uh, 
somebody has to,

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.766
somebody has to do something.

00:02:58.766 --> 00:03:01.166
We have to do something.

00:03:01.166 --> 00:03:09.299
And when I say something, I am 
complaining, because I want a very 
strong and aggressive

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:17.566
policy in population, if this country is 
going to be a country, a livable country 
within 20 years.

00:03:17.566 --> 00:03:24.332
[Music]

00:03:24.333 --> 00:03:28.566
[Narrator:] El Salvador has the highest 
population density in Latin America

00:03:28.566 --> 00:03:31.866
and one of the highest population 
growth rates in the world.

00:03:31.866 --> 00:03:35.232
There are three and half million people here now,

00:03:35.233 --> 00:03:41.266
and if something is not done, there will be seven million in 20 years.

00:03:41.266 --> 00:03:46.966
Already one can see what this might mean in 
terms of human degradation.

00:03:46.966 --> 00:03:51.499
[Music]

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:56.300
Although El Salvador does not have an 
official population policy,

00:03:56.300 --> 00:04:00.066
people like Dr. Madrigal are working to 
meet the challenge.

00:04:00.066 --> 00:04:04.099
In the meantime, human tragedies 
occur.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:08.500
[Doctor:] I can't tell you what my name 
is or show you my face,

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:10.966
or tell you the name of the hospital 
we're in.

00:04:10.966 --> 00:04:13.799
But I really want you to see this. It's terrible.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:18.233
This girl is Ann Marie and she's been 
here for about six weeks,

00:04:18.233 --> 00:04:20.866
laying very close to death from an 
illegal abortion.

00:04:20.866 --> 00:04:26.499
This is not a unique case, we have 
more than 60,000 cases like this a 
year,

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.033
and this is one country alone.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:33.866
As a doctor, I feel that if family planning 
services were more widely available,

00:04:33.866 --> 00:04:35.966
tragedies like this would never happen.

00:04:35.966 --> 00:04:40.332
[Narrator:] The great number of illegal 
abortions throughout Latin America and 
the risks taken

00:04:40.333 --> 00:04:45.533
by women who seek them is powerful 
proof of the desire by these women

00:04:45.533 --> 00:04:47.333
for a way to control the size of their 
families.

00:04:47.333 --> 00:04:51.899
Dr. Vernon Madrigal wants them to have an 
alternative to butchering.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:55.466
Among his many interests is female sterilization.

00:04:55.466 --> 00:04:58.999
[Dr. Madrigal:] This lady is a 32 years old lady.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:06.933
She has had six children ages from 11, 
I think, to five years old.

00:05:06.933 --> 00:05:15.533
And she's been taking pills in the last 
five years and she's so nervous, and 
she's so anxious too,

00:05:15.533 --> 00:05:23.299
about the problem that she decided to ask us to 
sterilize her.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:33.366
And we are doing it with a new method called 
laparoscopic tubal ligation.

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:35.532
I am the grantee of Pathfinder.

00:05:35.533 --> 00:05:42.533
So we are waiting for the government application and Pathfinder will provide the funds

00:05:42.533 --> 00:05:48.033
to those 300 tubal ligations in one year.

00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:48.799
Okay.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:52.066
[The doctor speaks in Spanish to the 
other medical staff.]

00:05:52.066 --> 00:05:54.632
She is under local anesthesia.

00:05:54.633 --> 00:05:59.533
She's not under general anesthesia, 
which represents a great advantage,

00:05:59.533 --> 00:06:04.766
because the lady can be operated with 
local anesthesia and then go home in 
four hours.

00:06:04.766 --> 00:06:09.132
[Narrator:] Dr. Madrigal got his laparoscope from 
the Pathfinder Fund, an American foundation

00:06:09.133 --> 00:06:12.233
concerned with population in developing 
countries.

00:06:12.233 --> 00:06:17.933
Along with Pathfinder and other 
groups, the Agency for International 
Development, AID,

00:06:17.933 --> 00:06:22.866
the largest source of assistance and 
funding in the field, is helping in an 
international assault

00:06:22.866 --> 00:06:25.432
upon the most pressing problem of the 
20th century.

00:06:25.433 --> 00:06:28.166
[Dr. Madrigal:] Okay.

00:06:28.166 --> 00:06:48.699
[A man and woman converse in 
Spanish.]

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:51.733
[Bill Flexner:] Some places in El Salvador are 
very difficult to get to.

00:06:51.733 --> 00:06:55.866
But getting there is part of winning the battle in 
health and family planning.

00:06:55.866 --> 00:06:59.766
The nurse that I came with, came because 
there's a problem of health within the family.

00:06:59.766 --> 00:07:04.699
After she tried to resolve this problem, 
she would talk to the family about 
preventive medicine

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:06.266
and family planning.

00:07:06.266 --> 00:07:08.932
AID is supporting her in this effort.

00:07:08.933 --> 00:07:15.699
[A nurse makes a presentation to a 
group of people gathered outdoors.]

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:20.300
[Narrator:] Sex education is an important part of 
the population program in El Salvador.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:24.533
In a few years these children will be in 
the prime reproductive age group,

00:07:24.533 --> 00:07:30.099
and then will have the knowledge to 
make intelligent decisions about family 
size.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:35.666
[A Filipino man speaks to a gathering 
of people.]

00:07:35.666 --> 00:07:39.332
[Narrator:] On the other side of the 
world, the governor of a Philippine 
province spends

00:07:39.333 --> 00:07:43.099
spends 30 percent of his time talking 
about family planning.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:47.666
Like Dr. Madrigal, governor Sam Luis 
is convinced that unchecked 
population growth

00:07:47.666 --> 00:07:54.032
is the greatest threat to his country.

00:07:54.033 --> 00:07:58.833
In the Philippines, one finds the 
problems of El Salvador reflected on a 
huge scale.

00:07:58.833 --> 00:08:02.966
In 1970, the government established a population 
policy.

00:08:02.966 --> 00:08:07.532
The result? In a short time the 
Philippines has developed a diverse, 
far-reaching

00:08:07.533 --> 00:08:12.599
family planning program, potentially 
one of the most effective in Southeast 
Asia.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:18.566
With help from international agencies, 
large input from AID, and the energetic 
efforts

00:08:18.566 --> 00:08:23.132
of Philippine officials and volunteers, 
the challenge is finally being faced.

00:08:23.133 --> 00:08:24.933
Is it too late?

00:08:24.933 --> 00:08:26.999
No one can say for sure.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:31.500
A traditional agricultural economy is giving way to 
industrialization.

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:36.000
The country is in the throes of a vast 
migration from farms to cities.

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:39.466
Manila is overcrowded and mired in smog.

00:08:39.466 --> 00:08:42.799
And its condo slums are among the worst in the 
world.

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:52.666
[Mrs. Aldaba-Lim:] Our statistics show 
today that more than 70 percent of our 
people belong to the poverty line,

00:08:52.666 --> 00:08:55.099
live within the poverty line.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:59.933
I know for a fact that there are 1.5 
million families in the Philippines

00:08:59.933 --> 00:09:03.333
who live below the subsistence level.

00:09:03.333 --> 00:09:12.833
And with this growth rate of 3.1 of 
Philippine population, you can just 
imagine how disastrous

00:09:12.833 --> 00:09:17.333
this would be for the future of our social and 
economic development.

00:09:17.333 --> 00:09:20.933
[Doug Larson:] As a Peace Corp 
volunteer here in the Philippines,

00:09:20.933 --> 00:09:23.799
you see many different developmental 
projects.

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:29.233
There are projects in agriculture, 
education, infrastructure,

00:09:29.233 --> 00:09:35.333
and yet all of these projects are 
diminished because of the vast 
population problem in this country.

00:09:35.333 --> 00:09:40.133
So I feel as a volunteer working here, 
it's been very rewarding to be in this 
kind of program that's

00:09:40.133 --> 00:09:42.233
that's at the crux of the matter.

00:09:42.233 --> 00:09:47.799
[Children sing a song in class.]

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:51.000
[Narrator:] Children too are at the crux of the 
matter.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:56.000
In a class on population awareness in 
an elementary school in Cabanatuan 
City,

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:58.600
second grade students play a game:

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:04.033
how many of them can fit into a limited 
space before the overcrowding 
becomes unbearable.

00:10:04.033 --> 00:10:12.033
How far can they be pressed before 
the game suddenly becomes unfunny.

00:10:12.033 --> 00:10:17.566
[Gov. San Luis:] God created man and all the beings on this earth.

00:10:17.566 --> 00:10:21.599
And by nature they're all selfish as God created has created it.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:27.533
And it is rather definitive that God has 
given us this in order that we survive.

00:10:27.533 --> 00:10:30.866
So every month I need to be selfish.

00:10:30.866 --> 00:10:38.932
And in our family planning program 
we're exploiting the selfishness of man

00:10:38.933 --> 00:10:41.899
in order that we can push through our 
family planning program.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:50.900
Why, because we know very well that 
over and above the laws of God, the 
laws of society,

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:54.166
is the law of the stomach.

00:10:54.166 --> 00:11:01.666
which is one of the [?] of man, the law 
of the stomach.

00:11:01.666 --> 00:11:05.132
So if you go to the barrios,

00:11:05.133 --> 00:11:11.866
and tell the people there in the barrios 
about how you can help the world, 
your country,

00:11:11.866 --> 00:11:13.866
by embracing family planning.

00:11:13.866 --> 00:11:16.466
They would not listen to you.

00:11:16.466 --> 00:11:22.066
But if you tell them, you help, if you  
embrace the family planning program, 
you'll be helping your children.

00:11:22.066 --> 00:11:25.066
In order that they will not be 
undernourished,

00:11:25.066 --> 00:11:27.499
in order that they will be able to go 
school.

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:32.666
So that you can give them a higher 
degree of education.

00:11:32.666 --> 00:11:37.366
It would be a very effective way, much more 
effective.

00:11:37.366 --> 00:11:43.032
And that is what we are learning.

00:11:43.033 --> 00:11:46.566
[A man and woman walking together 
call out to villagers, speaking Tagalog]

00:11:46.566 --> 00:11:50.832
[Narrator:] When Governor Sam Luis 
began his family planning programs in 
Laguna,

00:11:50.833 --> 00:11:53.099
he met resistance from the Catholic 
Church.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:58.633
Now the Responsible Parenthood 
Council, a Catholic organization, is 
working on population.

00:11:58.633 --> 00:12:02.599
Volunteer couples visit people in their homes to 
discuss the rhythm method.

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:07.500
In Cavite Province, Commander Borja and his 
wife have made more than 50 such visits.

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:11.933
How are they doing? Pretty good, says the 
Commander. So far, nobody's pregnant.

00:12:11.933 --> 00:12:20.866
[Voices speaking an African language]

00:12:20.866 --> 00:12:24.899
The home visit approach to family planning has 
no national boundaries.

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:33.300
In the mining town of Bomi Hills, in 
Liberia, Philip Koikoi

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:36.700
has been a professional visitor for four 
years.

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:42.633
In that time he's called on house after 
house on behalf of the Family Planning 
Association of Liberia,

00:12:42.633 --> 00:12:46.399
explaining to parents how they can 
restrict the size of their families.

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:50.233
Later, many of these people have 
shown up at the Bomi Hills Clinic,

00:12:50.233 --> 00:12:53.933
which dispenses a large assortment of 
birth prevention devices.

00:12:53.933 --> 00:13:06.833
[Music]

00:13:06.833 --> 00:13:12.633
Liberia has a relatively small population and is not 
yet embroiled in a population crisis.

00:13:12.633 --> 00:13:15.666
But the infant mortality rate here is 
high,

00:13:15.666 --> 00:13:23.166
and mother-child health care is below 
an acceptable standard.

00:13:23.166 --> 00:13:26.832
Though the government has no official 
population policy,

00:13:26.833 --> 00:13:31.666
the Family Planning Association of 
Liberia, a private group supported by 
the International

00:13:31.666 --> 00:13:37.532
Planned Parenthood Federation, 
supplies family planning services for 
those who wish them,

00:13:37.533 --> 00:13:41.566
emphasizes the health and welfare of 
mothers and babies,

00:13:41.566 --> 00:13:45.799
and instructs women on the proper 
spacing of children.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:56.400
[Music]

00:13:56.400 --> 00:14:03.266
[Nurse:] Three scoops of lactic in here and you put it up, water up to six ounces,

00:14:03.266 --> 00:14:05.599
and that's how much the baby's 
supposed to have.

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:07.766
Okay.

00:14:07.766 --> 00:14:10.432
Now make sure the water is boiled,

00:14:10.433 --> 00:14:18.499
and before you come to feed the baby, you wash your hands.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:22.833
[Narrator:] Mr. William Hill, 
Administrative Secretary to the Family 
Planning Association of Liberia,

00:14:22.833 --> 00:14:29.833
came to the University of Chicago to 
study Advanced Techniques in 
Population Communication.

00:14:29.833 --> 00:14:34.799
Mr. Hill's training in Chicago was part 
of a huge effort in manpower 
development,

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:37.133
central to the worldwide population 
movement.

00:14:37.133 --> 00:14:44.533
Over the next 10 years the movement needs 
more than 50,000 physicians, 150,000 nurses,

00:14:44.533 --> 00:14:48.633
100,000 health and family planning 
home visitors,

00:14:48.633 --> 00:14:54.833
thousands more medical and social 
workers, health and family life 
educators, demographers,

00:14:54.833 --> 00:15:00.166
behavioral scientists, and 
communications and training experts.

00:15:00.166 --> 00:15:06.232
[Man holding video camera:] If it's a face, as it is a [?] face, you should have the eyes in the middle.

00:15:06.233 --> 00:15:09.966
If you look at it...

00:15:09.966 --> 00:15:12.466
[Narrator:] India.

00:15:12.466 --> 00:15:18.932
After mainland China, the most populous country 
on earth, over half a billion people.

00:15:18.933 --> 00:15:25.733
If the growth rate is not checked, there will be 
more than a billion people by the year 2000.

00:15:25.733 --> 00:15:27.899
The effort here has been enormous,

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:32.066
the oldest and one of the largest 
official family planning programs in the 
world.

00:15:32.066 --> 00:15:36.066
Twenty years of labor by hundreds of thousands 
of people.

00:15:36.066 --> 00:15:42.032
The goal: lower the birthrate by 40 
percent over the next 10 years.

00:15:42.033 --> 00:15:47.866
In India they use the cafeteria 
approach, making a wide range of birth 
prevention methods

00:15:47.866 --> 00:15:53.599
easily available: sterilization, 
intrauterine devices, condoms, and 
other conventional contraceptives,

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:55.966
including pills in selected projects.

00:15:55.966 --> 00:15:59.632
However, sterilization is the mainstay of the 
program.

00:15:59.633 --> 00:16:05.699
In the city of Coonoor in Kerala state, 
one of the great innovations of the 
Indian effort,

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:11.800
a vasectomy camp, an intensive 
campaign to perform more than 15,000 
operations in 30 days.

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:16.533
[Dr. Bernard Coehlo:] This is where all 
the people come for the vasectomy 
operation. Here.

00:16:16.533 --> 00:16:21.133
[Background conversation.]

00:16:21.133 --> 00:16:28.666
And now we go to the central room.

00:16:28.666 --> 00:16:32.499
This is the control room where all the activities 
are controlled.

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:36.300
Actually this is the health center of the camp.

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:46.600
These are the hospitals responsible for 
the camp.

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:50.433
Here we find all the people lined up for the 
operation.

00:16:50.433 --> 00:16:53.666
They are coming from all over the district.

00:16:53.666 --> 00:16:57.832
And not only from this district, but other 
places also.

00:16:57.833 --> 00:17:03.933
[Doctor speaks in local language to the 
men in line. ]

00:17:03.933 --> 00:17:05.099
[Dr. Coehlo:] His name is Sangara.

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.733
He is 38 years old.

00:17:06.733 --> 00:17:10.733
He says he has three children.

00:17:10.733 --> 00:17:15.199
His wife is 30 years old.

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:17.033
Why do you come here?

00:17:17.033 --> 00:17:21.766
[Man answers in local language.]

00:17:21.766 --> 00:17:23.799
He says he doesn't want any more 
children.

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:28.800
He has three already.

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:36.666
He says his wife is willing, and he has 
no objections nor does his wife have 
any objections

00:17:36.666 --> 00:17:40.099
to the operation.

00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:43.700
[Narrator:] The operation takes less than 10 
minutes.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:46.833
It can be performed with scarcely the loss of a 
single drop of blood.

00:17:46.833 --> 00:17:52.966
One camp in Gujarat state, doctors 
perform the incredible number

00:17:52.966 --> 00:17:55.932
of 223,000 vasectomies in 60 days.

00:17:55.933 --> 00:18:02.733
[Music]

00:18:02.733 --> 00:18:05.999
There's a carnival atmosphere at the massive 
camps.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:11.800
Programs of live entertainment, songs and dances about the need for family planning...

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:18.300
prizes, inducements, awards. A whole people is behind this effort.

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:22.433
And Indians regard family planning as a patriotic 
duty.

00:18:22.433 --> 00:18:30.266
[Chanting]

00:18:30.266 --> 00:18:35.766
In 1971, the Indian Parliament legalized 
abortion as a maternal health measure,

00:18:35.766 --> 00:18:38.899
part of a pattern of changing laws 
throughout the world.

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:43.500
In Bombay, the world's first hospital 
devoted solely to family planning,

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:48.666
surgeons have devised a method of 
performing an abortion and a 
tubectomy at the same time.

00:18:48.666 --> 00:18:52.566
The Bombay program is the brainchild 
of Dr. Datta Pai.

00:18:52.566 --> 00:18:58.599
[Dr. Datta Pai:] You know this is a 
fantastic station, that in more than 
700,000 people pass everyday,

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:04.133
and it is here that the family planning history was 
made.

00:19:04.133 --> 00:19:11.099
In a city that there was only one sterilization per day, after setting up an operation here, down here,

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:16.900
we started doing 100, 200, 300 
operations every day.

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:28.666
[Music]

00:19:28.666 --> 00:19:31.899
[Narrator:] Centuries ago Arab tribes 
discovered that if a small pebble is 
placed

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:38.266
in the uterus of a female camel, that 
camel will not become pregnant.

00:19:38.266 --> 00:19:42.699
The Tunisian Institute of Family 
Planning and Maternal Child Health 
has chosen the camel,

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:49.100
the first animal to practice family 
planning, as the symbol of its program,

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:52.800
and the bearer of an important 
message to the Tunisian people.

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:58.000
[Music]

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:02.600
Tunisian Family Planning officials meet 
with representatives of foreign 
agencies

00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:04.100
concerned with population.

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:08.833
A doctor from the United Nations World 
Health Organization, a nurse-midwife 
from the

00:20:08.833 --> 00:20:13.466
Swedish International Development 
Authority, a demographer from the 
Population Council,

00:20:13.466 --> 00:20:18.466
representatives of AID and doctors, 
communicators, and demographers

00:20:18.466 --> 00:20:19.132
from other groups.

00:20:19.133 --> 00:20:23.466
They're meeting such as this in all the 
countries committed to population 
action.

00:20:23.466 --> 00:20:25.866
The challenge is worldwide.

00:20:25.866 --> 00:20:29.966
Response is international.

00:20:29.966 --> 00:20:38.132
Standing in the courtyard of the great 
mosque of Kairouan, Imam Mohamed 
Ali Trad

00:20:38.133 --> 00:20:40.933
says that family planning is not 
contrary to Islam,

00:20:40.933 --> 00:20:44.999
and it is necessary for economic 
development of the Tunisian nation.

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:49.733
Religious leaders throughout the world are 
conscious of the population project.

00:20:49.733 --> 00:20:53.833
And many of them have found that the 
idea of family planning is consistent

00:20:53.833 --> 00:20:56.299
with their religious principles.

00:20:56.300 --> 00:21:07.666
[Imam speaks]

00:21:07.666 --> 00:21:11.899
The role of women in Arab society is 
changing. Many have rejected their 
traditional role

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:14.900
and now practice family planning.

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:19.300
Dr. Bin Sheikh, a leader in the struggle 
for women's rights and the first female 
doctor

00:21:19.300 --> 00:21:25.166
in Tunisia, devotes all of her time to 
family planning counseling and clinical 
work.

00:21:25.166 --> 00:21:36.332
[Nurse walks through a hospital ward, 
speaking Arabic as she greets 
patients.]

00:21:36.333 --> 00:21:42.166
In Tunisia, as in many other countries, the post-
partum approach has been extremely successful.

00:21:42.166 --> 00:21:47.866
Immediately following the delivery of a 
child, women are especially responsive 
to a visit

00:21:47.866 --> 00:21:56.966
by a family planning worker, providing 
information on contraceptive methods.

00:21:56.966 --> 00:22:02.832
But it is not enough to confine the work to clinics 
or to wait for people to appear.

00:22:02.833 --> 00:22:09.066
Family planning workers must visit 
remote areas, bringing information and 
services and

00:22:09.066 --> 00:22:11.799
a special kind of human understanding.

00:22:11.800 --> 00:22:16.933
The key to all family planning programs is the 
winning of acceptance.

00:22:16.933 --> 00:22:21.233
Will the women who are contacted accept the 
methods that are available?

00:22:21.233 --> 00:22:26.299
The approach is the same everywhere, 
in Tunisia, in South Korea,

00:22:26.300 --> 00:22:27.633
in every country in the world.

00:22:27.633 --> 00:22:29.733
One woman must talk to another.

00:22:29.733 --> 00:22:34.566
They must be sympathetic and friendly.

00:22:34.566 --> 00:22:41.699
[Local language spoken]

00:22:41.700 --> 00:22:45.700
The home visit in a rural area is like a 
ritual.

00:22:45.700 --> 00:22:52.766
The lonely walk, the greeting, the establishment of rapport, the opening of the briefcase,

00:22:52.766 --> 00:22:56.532
the display, an explanation of available 
devices.

00:22:56.533 --> 00:23:05.466
[Visiting nurse explains family planning options, speaking local language.]

00:23:05.466 --> 00:23:09.899
The women who do this work are a new breed of 
missionaries.

00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:12.066
The often speak of their reward,

00:23:12.066 --> 00:23:16.299
the sense of personal accomplishment when they win another woman over,

00:23:16.300 --> 00:23:20.100
when they achieve the breakthrough 
called "acceptance."

00:23:20.100 --> 00:23:22.500
[Music]

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:29.000
South Korea, more than 32 million 
people, a rapidly developing nation 
that has reduced

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:32.033
its growth rate by one third in 10 years.

00:23:32.033 --> 00:23:36.499
The goal for 1976, another one-quarter 
decrease.

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:41.233
In the streets of Seoul, one senses the 
dynamism and discipline of a people 
whose country

00:23:41.233 --> 00:23:46.199
has been transformed from rural to 
urban, from farming to an industrial 
power

00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:47.833
in a few short years.

00:23:47.833 --> 00:23:53.199
South Korea is one of the few success stories in 
the battle against an exploding population.

00:23:53.200 --> 00:23:57.500
The Korean accomplishment is a valid 
inspiration to the developing world,

00:23:57.500 --> 00:24:00.633
for it was not easily achieved.

00:24:00.633 --> 00:24:07.333
[Family around a table speaking 
Korean]

00:24:07.333 --> 00:24:10.133
The first year birthday party of a male child.

00:24:10.133 --> 00:24:15.699
This is a traditional ceremony in Korea, 
where the preference for sons was 
long a barrier

00:24:15.700 --> 00:24:18.966
family planning, but the country is 
changing.

00:24:18.966 --> 00:24:22.566
Urbanization is leading to a desire for smaller 
families.

00:24:22.566 --> 00:24:24.666
Women are becoming better educated.

00:24:24.666 --> 00:24:28.499
But the key factor is the commitment of the 
Korean government.

00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:31.800
It has taken 10 years of hard work to 
turn the growth-rate statistics around.

00:24:31.800 --> 00:24:40.466
[The baby begins crying.]

00:24:40.466 --> 00:24:47.732
Faced by population disaster a decade 
ago, Korea has mounted an extensive 
program,

00:24:47.733 --> 00:24:54.199
training communication, collection and 
use of demographic data, a network of 
mother's clubs

00:24:54.200 --> 00:24:59.300
for family planning promotion, and even a manufacturer of condoms,

00:24:59.300 --> 00:25:01.933
as in this factory at Onyang.

00:25:01.933 --> 00:25:05.866
[Music]

00:25:05.866 --> 00:25:10.166
[Dr. Ravenholt:] Since 1965, the United States 
through the Agency for International Development

00:25:10.166 --> 00:25:14.499
has provided rapidly increasing 
support for population and family 
planning programs

00:25:14.500 --> 00:25:16.633
throughout the developing world.

00:25:16.633 --> 00:25:22.499
These funds, channeled through many organizations, now especially the United Nations,

00:25:22.500 --> 00:25:29.333
have gone for a broad scope of action 
including research and provision of 
contraceptives such as these,

00:25:29.333 --> 00:25:36.199
especially oral contraceptives provided 
so that poor women and couples in the 
developing countries

00:25:36.200 --> 00:25:45.633
can control their fertility as they wish, 
to improve their health and well-being.

00:25:45.633 --> 00:25:51.299
[Narrator:] The birth of a child is always a miracle, 
even to those who have seen it many times.

00:25:51.300 --> 00:25:57.900
In South Korea today, a birth is a more joyous 
miracle then in most developing countries,

00:25:57.900 --> 00:26:04.433
because as a result of an intensive program of 
family planning, the future of a child is far brighter.

00:26:04.433 --> 00:26:08.166
There should be no starvation for this Korean 
baby.

00:26:08.166 --> 00:26:13.332
The chance is good that he will have 
an education, a job in a dynamic 
economy,

00:26:13.333 --> 00:26:18.066
a decent environment, and perhaps 
most important, a sense of dignity.

00:26:18.066 --> 00:26:26.532
If such things can happen in Korea, then they can 
be made to happen everywhere.

00:26:26.533 --> 00:26:29.266
In Latin America a child dies.

00:26:29.266 --> 00:26:31.732
In Korea a child is born.

00:26:31.733 --> 00:26:36.699
Children are the future and their destiny is in our 
hands.

00:26:36.700 --> 00:26:41.466
If the population challenge is met, then the future 
holds great promise.

00:26:41.466 --> 00:26:47.232
If it is not met, well, it must be met, 
because when we speak of population,

00:26:47.233 --> 00:26:55.099
we are speaking of the future of the 
human race.

00:26:55.100 --> 00:27:20.140
[Music]

